lib/scorer/lanes/derived.ts:94` then falls back to `projection.generatedAt`, which the adjacent comment (derived.ts:88-90) admits is near-now on every run and exempts skills from the haircut.\n**Risk:** any skill whose derived block goes through the v2 sync path loses per-skill freshness and scores as perpetually fresh. **Fix class:** code-small (accept `generated_at` in the projection's timestamp coalesce, both SQLite and filesystem branches, plus a regression test). **Interlock:** tri-036.\n\nCANDIDATES:\n - .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/derived.ts\n===== ROW 19 | basename_only | total: 1\nDOC: specs/system-deep-loop/036-deep-loop-innovation/001-research-inputs-and-architecture/002-deep-loop-effectiveness-and-fanout/research/iterations/iteration-003.md LINE: 3228\nCIT: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature_catalog/feature_catalog.md:472\nCONTEXT:\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature_catalog/feature_catalog.md:464:### Coverage-graph fuzzy merge\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature_catalog/feature_catalog.md:468:Adds deterministic fuzzy-merge query helpers for near-duplicate coverage nodes without mutating graph rows.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature_catalog/feature_catalog.md:472:`findSimilarNodes()` compares names inside one namespace and category, while `findConsolidationCandidates()` returns candidate clusters and leftovers; callers decide whether to merge results.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature_catalog/feature_catalog.md:476:See [`coverage-graph/coverage-graph-fuzzy-merge.md`](coverage_graph/coverage_graph_fuzzy_merge.md) for full implementation and validation file listings.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature_catalog/feature_catalog.md:564:### Round-state JSONL\nCANDIDATES:\n - specs/sk-doc/z_archive/016-create-diff-mode/013-catalog-playbook-snippet-denumbering/002-migration-tooling-and-dry-run/tooling/fixtures/happy/feature_catalog/feat